\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Ere God had built the mountains,
\par Or raised the fruitful hills;
\par Before He filled the fountains
\par That feed the running rills;
\par In me, from everlasting,
\par The wonderful I AM
\par Found pleasures never wasting,
\par And Wisdom is my name.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  When, like a tent to dwell in,
\par He spread the skies abroad,
\par And swathed about the swelling
\par Of ocean's mighty flood,
\par He wrought by weight and measure,
\par And I was with Him then;
\par Myself the Father's pleasure,
\par And mine, the sons of men.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thus Wisdom's words discover
\par Thy glory and Thy grace,
\par Thou everlasting lover
\par Of our unworthy race:
\par Thy gracious eye surveyed us
\par Ere stars were seen above;
\par In wisdom Thou hast made us,
\par And died for us in love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. And couldst Thou be delighted
\par With creatures such as we,
\par Who, when we saw Thee, slighted
\par And nailed Thee to a tree?
\par Unfathomable wonder,
\par And mystery divine;
\par The voice that speaks in thunder
\par Says: Sinner, I am thine!
\par 
\par  \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

